{
  "_readme": [
    "Direction lexicon. Decides whether a news item implies prices UP or DOWN.",
    "",
    "This exists because the news feed scores relevance, not direction, and",
    "direction matching is the single check that stops a plausible-sounding but",
    "wrong story being attached to a move. Pass 1 of the historic research had",
    "no direction check and mislabelled accordingly.",
    "",
    "Deterministic and hand-tuned, in the same style as themes.json, so it costs",
    "nothing to run and can always be explained. Weights are relative, not",
    "absolute: what matters is which side wins, not by how much.",
    "",
    "Add terms as the market changes. Keep them lowercase. Phrases are matched",
    "on word boundaries, so 'restart' will not fire inside 'restarting' unless",
    "you add the stem."
  ],
